", "text": "surveillance", "sentence": "The shop uses surveillance cameras."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "surveillance"}'::jsonb),('spell',89,'s089',12,'spelling','{"type": "spell", "text": "acquiesce", "sentence": "He chose to acquiesce rather than argue."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "acquiesce"}'::jsonb),('spell',90,'s090',12,'spelling','{"type": "spell", "text": "camaraderie", "sentence": "The team shared a strong camaraderie."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "camaraderie"}'::jsonb),('spell',91,'s091',12,'spelling','{"type": "spell", "text": "connoisseur", "sentence": "She is a connoisseur of fine tea."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "connoisseur"}'::jsonb),('spell',92,'s092',12,'spelling','{"type": "spell", "text": "idiosyncrasy", "sentence": "Humming is one of his idiosyncrasies."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "idiosyncrasy"}'::jsonb),('spell',93,'s093',12,'spelling','{"type": "spell", "text": "mnemonic", "sentence": "A mnemonic can help you remember the order."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "mnemonic"}'::jsonb),('spell',94,'s094',12,'spelling','{"type": "spell", "text": "pharmaceutical", "sentence": "He works for a pharmaceutical company."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "pharmaceutical"}'::jsonb),('spell',95,'s095',12,'spelling','{"type": "spell", "text": "reconnaissance", "sentence": "The soldiers went on a reconnaissance mission."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "reconnaissance"}'::jsonb),('spell',96,'s096',12,'spelling','{"type": "spell", "text": "silhouette", "sentence": "We saw the silhouette of a tree at dusk."}'::jsonb,'{"value": "silhouette"}'::jsonb),('fluency',1,'f1',1,'fluency','{"type": "fluency", "passages": [{"key": "A", "label": "Easier text (about Years 2 to 3)", "title": "The Lost Kite", "text": "Sam and his sister Mia went to the park on a windy morning. Sam had a bright red kite with a long tail. He held the string tightly and ran across the grass. The kite lifted into the air and danced above the trees. Mia clapped her hands and laughed. Then a strong gust of wind pulled the string out of Sam''s fingers. The kite spun round and flew away over the hedge. Sam and Mia chased it down the path. They looked under the bushes and behind the old shed. At last Mia pointed to the tall oak tree. The kite was hanging from a high branch, swinging in the breeze. A kind man with a ladder helped them to get it down. Sam thanked him and wrapped the string around his hand twice. This time he would not let go.", "words": 142}, {"key": "B", "label": "Middle text (about Years 4 to 5)", "title": "The Harbour at Dawn", "text": "Every morning, before the sun had risen, the fishing boats left the harbour. Maria liked to sit on the wall and watch them go. The air smelled of salt, and the gulls circled above the water. Her grandfather had worked on these boats for forty years. He still woke up before dawn, even though he had stopped fishing. Today he sat next to her with a flask of hot tea. He pointed out the boats one by one and told her their names. The little blue boat belonged to a man called Tomas. Tomas always came home with the biggest catch of fish. As the engines faded away, the sea turned from grey to gold. Maria took out her notebook and began to draw the scene. She wanted to remember every small detail. Next month her family was moving to a big city, a long way from the sea. She did not know when she would see the harbour again. Her grandfather smiled and said that the sea would always be waiting for her. Maria drew one more gull and then closed the book.", "words": 184}, {"key": "C", "label": "Harder text (about Year 6 and above)", "title": "The Clockmaker''s Apprentice", "text": "When Elias first entered the workshop, the constant ticking of hundreds of clocks seemed almost overwhelming. Shelves stretched from floor to ceiling, crowded with brass dials and delicate springs. The clockmaker was a stern woman who barely looked up from her work. She explained that precision was everything, because a single misplaced cog could silence an entire clock. For weeks, Elias did nothing except sweep the floor and polish the metal cases. He wondered whether he would ever be trusted with a real repair. Then, one stormy evening, a damaged pocket watch arrived from a customer who had travelled a long way. The clockmaker handed Elias a tiny screwdriver and a magnifying glass without saying a word. His hands trembled as he lifted the back of the watch. He took a deep breath and remembered everything he had seen her do. Slowly and carefully, he began to work. The rain hammered against the window, but he did not notice it. After several hours, the watch gave a faint, hesitant tick. The clockmaker looked at it for a long moment, and then she nodded. It was the first time Elias had seen her smile.", "words": 193}]}'::jsonb,null),('pa_blend',1,'pa_blend01',1,'pa_blend','{"type": "pa", "mode": "pa_blend", "q": "Say the sounds, one every second: /k/ /a/ /t/. Then ask: What is the word?", "n": 1, "of": 10}'::jsonb,'{"accept": "cat"}'::jsonb),('pa_blend',2,'pa_blend02',2,'pa_blend','{"type": "pa", "mode": "pa_blend", "q": "/s/ /u/ /n/", "n": 2, "of": 10}'::jsonb,'{"accept": "sun"}'::jsonb),('pa_blend',3,'pa_blend03',3,'pa_blend','{"type": "pa", "mode": "pa_blend", "q": "/sh/ /i/ /p/", "n": 3, "of": 10}'::jsonb,'{"accept": "ship"}'::jsonb),('pa_blend',4,'pa_blend04',4,'pa_blend','{"type": "pa", "mode": "pa_blend", "q": "/f/ /r/ /o/ /g/", "n": 4, "of": 10}'::jsonb,'{"accept": "frog"}'::jsonb),('pa_blend',5,'pa_blend05',5,'pa_blend','{"type": "pa", "mode": "pa_blend", "q": "/s/ /t/ /o/ /p/", "n": 5, "of": 10}'::jsonb,'{"accept": "stop"}'::jsonb),('pa_blend',6,'pa_blend06',6,'pa_blend','{"type": "pa", "mode": "pa_blend", "q": "/b/ /l/ /a/ /ck/", "n": 6, "of": 10}'::jsonb,'{"accept": "black"}'::jsonb),('pa_blend',7,'pa_blend07',7,'pa_blend','{"type": "pa", "mode": "pa_blend", "q": "/s/ /p/ /l/ /a/ /sh/", "n": 7, "of": 10}'::jsonb,'{"accept": "splash"}'::jsonb),('pa_blend',8,'pa_blend08',8,'pa_blend','{"type": "pa", "mode": "pa_blend", "q": "/s/ /t/ /r/ /i/ /ng/", "n": 8, "of": 10}'::json